# GitHub no longer requires code owner review: the "protect main" ruleset
# (.github/rulesets/main.json) has require_code_owner_review false, by the
# owner's decision of 2026-11-23. Ordinary changes merge on the required checks
# plus the hive's AI reviewer.
#
# The two paths below still need the owner. What enforces that is the hive's
# own merge gate (auto_merge.human_merge_paths in the hive's config): it holds
# a pull request touching them with the needs-owner-merge label until a person
# merges it. This file only asks GitHub to request the owner's review on them.
#
# These lines must match owner_merge_paths in risk-config.json, and nothing
# else may be listed (no catch-all `*`): scripts/check-policies.mjs fails
# otherwise. docs/agent-boundaries.md explains it.

/.github/rulesets/                              @Danathar
/.github/CODEOWNERS                             @Danathar
